WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.635
-Guys, have you ever seen
a photo in the news

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.403
and think the headline
could be so much better?

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:08.341
I'll show you what I mean. It's
time for "News and Improved."

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:12.879
-♪ News and Improved ♪

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.381
-For example, check out
this first photo.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:18.351
The original headline was
"Trump Greets Supporters."

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.952
That headline could
definitely be improved,

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.420
because if you only looked
at the photo,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.788
the headline could have been,

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.691
"Drunk Friend Signals 'All Good'
from Back of Cop Car."

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:28.161
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.466
Check out this next photo here.
The original headline was,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.402
"Giuliani Gives
Press Conference,"

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.636
but if you only looked
at the photo,

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.104
the headline could have been,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:42.041
"Just For Men Urges Customers to
Follow the One Box a Day Rule."

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:45.177
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.580
Honestly, it looks like
soy sauce.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.083
-Yeah.
-Up next, this headline says,

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.618
"Biden Names
First Cabinet Pick."

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.153
The headline could have been,

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.556
"Man Tells Gripping Story
about Recent Prostate Exam."

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.558
See how it is? The headline --

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.292
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.461
The next headline was,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.163
"McConnell Proposes
Shifting Funds."

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.965
Come on.
The headline could have been,

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.366
"Turkey Gives Closing Argument

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.668
on Why He Should Be Spared
This Year."

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:11.938
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:18.311
This next headline was,
"Medvedev Wins Paris Masters."

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.645
The headline could have been,

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:23.750
"Man Vows Never Again
to Go on Amazon While Drunk."

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.451
"The heck is it?

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.286
Tie rack?"

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:28.387
Next headline was,

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.989
"Iowa Celebrates
After Winning Touchdown."

00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:32.392
Headline could have been,

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.527
"Iowa's had
the Time of Their Lives

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.763
and They've Never Felt
This Way Before."

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:40.132
[ Applause ]

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:43.703
The next headline was,
"Harris Briefed on Economy."

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.838
The headline could have been,
"Woman Starting to Worry

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.841
About Friend Who Went
to Bathroom 20 Minutes Ago."

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:52.478
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.748
Next headline was,
"NASA Teams Up with Space-X."

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:56.982
Headline could have been,

00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:00.085
"Old Navy Announces New
'Pandemic Chic' Line."

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:02.421
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:06.391
The next headline was, "Chinese
Demand for Crops Increases."

00:02:06.391 --> 00:02:07.827
Headline could have been,

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:11.430
"Man Again Miscalculates How
Much Pasta to Put in the Pot."

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.401
I don't know.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.369
That much? Way too much.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.604
Did you ever buy those --

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.240
I bet you bought one.
-What?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.808
-One of those --
They almost look like a ruler

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:24.977
or something like that,
that have holes in it,

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.479
and you put the pasta
in the holes

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.781
that measures out how much --

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.116
-Yeah, I know. No, no.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.450
-Have you bought one?
-No.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.819
-I think Questlove has.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.354
-Yeah, I just take a handful
of pasta, snap it in half,

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:37.290
and go for it.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.457
-Why do you snap it in half?

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:42.562
-I don't like super long
noodles, you know?

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.763
-You're in the wrong game, dude.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.165
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.401
You don't want to, like, do,
"Lady and the Tramp" stuff?

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.704
-I mean, nah, no,
especially not during COVID.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.839
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.406
-I'm talking about
with your family,

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.275
your wife, Michelle.
-I mean, yeah.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.211
Hey, man, anybody
can get sick now.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.913
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.047
No, man.

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:03.515
-That's the only way
I eat my pasta now.

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:04.883
-Oh, yeah?
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:07.086
There's one giant noodle
in a bowl,

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.389
and takes me and my wife
about three hours. Yeah.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.223
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:15.494
-Do you use a spoon to swirl
your pasta around the fork or --

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.196
-That is a good question. I --

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:20.066
Clearly, you don't,
'cause you have too short pasta.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.734
But --

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.636
But I --
Yeah, I started doing it,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.072
and it kind of used to make
my dad mad for some reason.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.340
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.775
It's like,
"Why are you getting mad?"

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:31.310
He's like, "No one does that.
You don't have to do that."

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.612
I go, "I don't have to do it,
but I'm doing it."

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.316
And then my mom was like,
"Jimmy's been to Italy,

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.051
so I think that's what they do."

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.785
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:40.953
So, yeah. It think
it was the thing like,

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:42.421
"Oh, Mr. Big Shot."
-Show off.

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.991
-"You going to teach me how
to eat pasta now, Mr. Big Shot,

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.326
huh? Go get me a beer!"

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:50.563
No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.665
Yeah, I'm just kidding.

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:57.637
This next headline was,
"Pompeo Visits Middle East."

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.872
Headline could have been,
"Dad Bans Sleepovers

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.341
After Getting Pranked
Into Gluing Hand To Head."

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:04.310
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.679
"Reginald!"

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.216
-[ Laughs ]
That's your kid's name?

00:04:11.216 --> 00:04:12.518
-Yeah, Reginald is the --

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:16.221
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.221 --> 00:04:18.858
"Reginald!

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:22.895
No more sleepovers."

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.496
Finally, this headline was,

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:27.666
"Rockefeller Center
Christmas Tree Arrives."

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:30.002
Headline could have been,
"Year Summed Up in Tree."

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.037
There you go.
That's all the time we have

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.072
for "News and Improved."

